{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NkJomWrU5uyyqc4NiXJKqw","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's my analysis of the test utilities:\n\n## Summary\n\n### 1. DiffTest Struct Definition (Full)\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5453/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`, lines 46-55:\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Field explanations:**\n- **Name**: Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n- **Args**: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- **Stdin**: Input data; nil means EOF immediately, empty non-nil slice ([]byte{}) also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin\n- **Env**: KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited environment; nil means inherit test process environment with LC_ALL=C applied as default override\n- **WorkDir**: Working directory for binary execution; defaults to t.TempDir() if empty\n- **ExitCode**: Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- **Normalize**: Slice of NormalizeFunc applied in order to stdout and stderr before comparison\n- **ExpectedFiles**: Map of relative paths to expected file contents for file-based comparison\n\n### 2. RunDiffTests Function Signature\nLines 83-90:\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n```\n\nTakes a test object, paths to Go and reference binaries, and a slice of test cases. Runs each DiffTest as a named subtest.\n\n### 3. BuildBinary Function Signature\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5453/pkg/testutils/build.go`, lines 16-27:\n\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n```\n\nCompiles the Go package at `dir` and returns the path to the compiled binary. The binary is placed in a temporary directory cleaned up when the test completes.\n\n### 4. Output File Comparison Mechanism\nYes, there is a mechanism for comparing files created by the binary. The `ExpectedFiles` field in DiffTest enables this.\n\nFiles are compared in the `checkExpectedFiles` function (lines 211-227):\n- Iterates over the `ExpectedFiles` map\n- For each relative path, constructs the full path within the WorkDir\n- Reads the actual file content with `os.ReadFile(fullPath)`\n- Compares actual bytes against expected bytes using `bytes.Equal()`\n- Fails the test if file is missing or content diverges\n\nThis comparison happens **after** stdout/stderr comparison in `runSubtest` (line 104).\n\n### 5. Other Relevant Types and Functions\n\n**NormalizeFunc type** (line 28):\n```go\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n```\nA named type alias for functions that transform raw output bytes before comparison.\n\n**Built-in Normalizer - TimestampNormalizer** (lines 57-72):\nReplaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder `<TIMESTAMP>`. Supports three patterns:\n- Syslog format: \"May 21 14:30:00\"\n- ISO format: \"2026-05-21 14:30:00\"\n- Time-only: \"14:30:00\"\n\n**ComposeNormalizers function** (lines 232-238):\n```go\nfunc ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\n```\nConvenience function for combining multiple normalizers into a single NormalizeFunc that applies them in order.\n\n**Helper Functions Used Internally:**\n- `buildEnv()`: Merges custom environment variables into inherited environment\n- `applyNormalizers()`: Applies all normalizer functions to both stdout and stderr\n- `compareOutputs()`: Compares stdout, stderr, and exit code between binaries\n- `formatDivergence()`: Creates detailed error message when outputs diverge"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9885cd55-a14f-42b5-88c0-58b53a0ce59f","uuid":"fe37f2bb-36ed-464e-9512-ee8ded18918c","timesta